PRISM Source-Available Evaluation Licence (Draft 0.1)

Copyright (c) 2026 Odin Loch / Imortek. All rights reserved.

1. Definitions
   "Software" means the PRISM source code, documentation, build scripts and
   any binaries built from them that are made available in this repository,
   excluding the third-party components listed in NOTICE and
   third_party/MANIFEST.toml, which remain under their own licences.
   "Licensor" means Odin Loch, trading as Imortek.
   "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
   licence.
   "Evaluation Purpose" means reading, auditing, building and running the
   Software internally to assess its fitness, security or correctness,
   including security accreditation and procurement review.

2. Grant
   Subject to this licence, the Licensor grants You a non-exclusive,
   non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free, revocable licence to
   (a) view and audit the source code of the Software;
   (b) build the Software from source and verify that the build reproduces
       published release artefacts; and
   (c) run the Software internally for an Evaluation Purpose for a period of
       ninety (90) days from first use, or longer if agreed in writing.

3. Restrictions
   You must not, without a separate written licence from the Licensor:
   (a) redistribute, publish, sell, lease, lend or sublicense the Software or
       any modified version of it, in source or binary form;
   (b) use the Software in production, for the benefit of third parties, or
       to provide a hosted or managed service;
   (c) remove or alter any copyright, licence or attribution notice; or
   (d) use the Software to build a competing product.
   Findings and reports that the Software produces about Your own code are
   Yours, and may be shared as You wish.

4. Modifications
   You may modify the Software only for an Evaluation Purpose. Modifications
   may not be distributed. If You send the Licensor feedback or patches, You
   grant the Licensor a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free
   licence to use them for any purpose.

5. Third-party components
   Third-party components keep their own licences (see NOTICE and
   third_party/MANIFEST.toml). Nothing in this licence restricts rights You
   have under those licences. External tools that PRISM invokes are not part
   of the Software and are not distributed with it.

6. No warranty
   To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Software is provided "as is",
   without warranty of any kind. A PRISM verdict is evidence, not a
   guarantee: read the report's NOTRUN, BOUNDED and HYPOTHESIS entries.
   Nothing in this licence excludes, restricts or modifies any right or
   remedy, or any guarantee, warranty or other term or condition, implied or
   imposed by the Australian Consumer Law (Schedule 2 of the Competition and
   Consumer Act 2010 (Cth)) or any other legislation that cannot lawfully be
   excluded or limited. Where liability can be limited, the Licensor's
   liability is limited, at its option, to resupplying the Software or
   paying the cost of having it resupplied.

7. Limitation of liability
   To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Licensor is not liable for
   any indirect, consequential, special or incidental loss, or loss of
   profit, revenue, data or goodwill, arising out of or in connection with
   the Software or this licence.

8. Termination
   This licence ends automatically if You breach it, and otherwise at the end
   of the evaluation period. On termination You must stop using the Software
   and delete all copies, except that You may keep reports it produced.

9. Governing law
   This licence is governed by the laws of [State/Territory — to be confirmed
   by counsel], Australia, and the parties submit to the non-exclusive
   jurisdiction of its courts.

10. Commercial licences
